    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full build passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field for owners.\n\n**What I added:**\n\n1. **`OwnerSegment` helper** (`model/OwnerSegment.java`) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility class that classifies an owner into its `<TIER>_<AREA>` segment:\n   - `TIER` = `PREMIUM` when membership level \u2265 3, else `STANDARD`.\n   - `AREA` = `METRO` when the locality is a known region (`NSW`, `VIC`, `QLD`), else `REGIONAL`.\n\n2. **`Owner.getOwnerSegment()`** \u2014 a derived read-only property that composes the segment from the existing `getMembershipLevel()` and `getLocality()` accessors (reusing them rather than recomputing), following the same pattern as the other derived getters (`getTimezone`, `getContactPreference`, etc.).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` schema property (readOnly, enum of the four values) to the Owner schema. This regenerates it onto `OwnerDto`, and MapStruct maps it by name from `getOwnerSegment()`, so it appears in the JSON response.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known Sydney/NSW owner, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown-city owner) pass, and the full build is green.\n\nI placed the \"known metro regions\" set in the segment helper since it's that classification's own concern, rather than overloading the existing `RegionTimezone`/`CityRegion` tables which serve different responsibilities.",
